    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608">

                <pb facs="0598" n="1332" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1332"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram received last night, regarding Lenz and missionary protection,
                    indicates a better spirit on the part of the Turkish Government than your
                    preceding telegram showed, and suggests that good management may avert proposed
                    formal demand for passports.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d608-f1"/> Impress firmly on
                    Turkish Government our right to be promptly answered as to just demands and our
                    confidence that answers will be satisfactory.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d608-f1" n="1" xml:id="d608-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram from Mr. Terrell of October 30, 1895, printed on <ref
                        target="#pg1314">page 1314</ref>.</p>
